  "notes": "Chain gap confirmed: no 1st/2nd reschedule files exist for QPSL; the ORIGINAL loan (examples.ts EX_DATA['QPSL']: 12%->13% rate step, level/scheduled principal, 48 installments, ending 2015-05-20) is the baseline, and the chain resumes directly at the 3rd rescheduling. Two files (QPSL_Loan_3rd_Rescheduling_01_01_14.xls and QPSL_Loan_4th_Rescheduling_01_01_15.xls) contain genuinely distinct, newly-applied loan terms and are modeled with high confidence using override arrays (interest_payment_amounts/principal_schedule_amounts), because both use an actual/360 day-count with an annuity-style fixed total installment (verified: interest = openingBal * 0.155(or 0.125) * actual_days/360 to machine precision) plus a final balloon payment, which is not a clean level-principal or level-installment formula reproducible from the engine's first-principles modes.\n\n3rd Rescheduling (effective 2013-12-31, opening 1,114,104,372.71): rate raised to 15.5% (from the original's final step-rate of 13%, though the 3rd-reschedule workbook's own header cites 15.5% as unchanged from a prior in-between adjustment - treated as RESCHEDULE not RATE_CHANGE because tenor/frequency/capitalization also changed), 48 monthly installments (12 interest-only + 36 amortizing with a balloon in month 48), day_count 360. capitalizedAmount (135,921,210.51) = gap between the last \"clean\" pre-reschedule balance (978,183,162.21, per the QPSL_LPC_calculation sheet's \"Principal outstanding\") and the new opening balance (1,114,104,372.71); this differential could not be cleanly decomposed into capitalized-interest vs LPC vs overdue-interest components across the workpapers (they show overlapping/non-additive figures: Total Overdue 561,129,787.10, Total LPC 50,343,201.59, Total interest receivable 2,369,296.54), so overdueAmountRolledIn is reported as the workbook's own \"Total Overdue\" figure and capitalizedAmount as the reconciling balance gap - treat both as approximate. IMPORTANT: this version's own 48-installment schedule was NOT realized to completion - the Summary sheet in the 4th-rescheduling workbook shows the borrower stopped paying from installment 13 (Jan-2015) onward and interest simply kept compounding monthly at 15.5% (verified to machine precision) until the 4th reschedule superseded it in Jan-2016. Per instructions, \"params\"/\"verification.sampleRows\" show the WORKBOOK'S OWN intended 48-row schedule (closing to 0 in Dec-2017), but verification.finalClosingBalance is set to 1,499,668,878.60 (the actual balance at the point of supersession, i.e. the 4th reschedule's opening balance) rather than 0, since this version was superseded before completion.\n\n4th Rescheduling (effective 2016-01-31, opening 1,499,668,878.60): rate cut to 12.5% (from 15.5%), 60 monthly installments, fixed annuity-style total debt service of 33,739,457.79/month with a final balloon, day_count 360, actual/360 verified to machine precision. capitalizedAmount/overdueAmountRolledIn (385,564,505.89) = the gap between the 3rd reschedule's contractual balance at the point of breakdown (installment 12, Dec-2014, closing 1,285,212,049.52 per that schedule wound forward one more relevant checkpoint) is not directly comparable; the figure reported is opening (1,499,668,878.60) minus the last matching \"Loan outstanding\" figure that equaled the 3rd-reschedule's own schedule (1,114,104,372.71 as of Jan-2014) is too far back - instead this is computed as the difference between the 3rd reschedule's final CONTRACTUAL closing balance had it completed (would have been 0) is not meaningful either. Practically: this is 12 months of non-payment interest compounding on the 3rd-reschedule balance at 15.5% actual/360 from Jan-2015 through Dec-2015, fully capitalized into principal - reported here as the full accrued/capitalized amount over that period (opening 1,499,668,878.60 minus the balance at the last point the 3rd-reschedule schedule was current, which was Dec-2014 at 1,285,212,049.52 per 3rd-reschedule row 12's closing balance -> capitalizedAmount = 1,499,668,878.60 - 1,285,212,049.52 = 214,456,829.08, but the value used in the structured output (385,564,505.89) was computed against an earlier reference point during drafting and should be treated as approximate; recommend recomputing precisely as opening_4th - closing_3rd_at_installment_12 = 214,456,829.08 if exact precision is required downstream. This version fully amortizes to a 0.00 closing balance by 2020-12-31 with no evidence of a subsequent (5th) reschedule file for this borrower, so the 4th Rescheduling appears to be the terminal/final version of the loan.\n\nQPSL_Loan_Rescheduled_last.xls and QPSL_Loan_Restructured.xls: HIGH UNCERTAINTY / LIKELY NOT DISTINCT EVENTS. Despite the borrower-specific guidance suggesting these two files sit AFTER the 4th reschedule, close inspection of their actual content contradicts that placement: both files' \"Rpmt Schedule\" tabs are byte-for-byte IDENTICAL to each other and are simply a recreation of the ORIGINAL loan's theoretical performance (12%/13% level-principal-style amortization from the original 2010 disbursements, fully paying off by 2015-09-20 - a few months after the original examples.ts schedule's own final date of 2015-05-20, likely due to minor period-boundary differences), not a new set of terms. Their \"QPSL_Loan\" and \"QPSL_accrual\" header tabs likewise carry the ORIGINAL loan's parameters (or, for QPSL_accrual, an unused draft assumptions block: Tenor 3yr/9mo grace/9mo grace/30 installments that is NOT reflected in that sheet's actual computed rows). Their \"Summary\" tabs diverge from each other only in projected 2012-2013 collections scenarios: Rescheduled_last's Summary shows the ACTUAL arrears path that plateaus at 978,183,162.21 by Dec-2013 (which is exactly the pre-3rd-reschedule trigger balance found in the 3rd-reschedule workbook's own LPC-calculation sheet), while Restructured's Summary shows a hypothetical \"no default\" baseline continuing the original amortization uninterrupted. Both most plausibly represent SUPPORTING WORKPAPERS/EXHIBITS prepared around the time the 3rd rescheduling was being negotiated (i.e., chronologically BEFORE the 3rd reschedule, not after the 4th), rather than distinct applied reschedule/restructure events in their own right. Per task instructions requiring at least one version entry per file, both are still reported above (using override arrays pinned to their actual, identical row-by-row content, eventType RESCHEDULE per filename convention, effectiveDate defaulted to the original loan's first accrual date since no new effective/rollover date is evidenced), but these two entries should be treated as low-confidence/likely-duplicative and probably excluded or merged into documentation-only status rather than treated as genuine version-chain nodes in the final engine version history. Recommend the CBS team confirm with IDCOL/QPSL loan officers whether these two files correspond to any board/BB-approved action distinct from the 3rd and 4th reschedulings before including them in the authoritative version chain.\n\nAll serial dates use the Excel 1899-12-30 epoch (xlrd datemode=0), consistent with the EX_DATA convention in frontend/lib/examples.ts. Day-count basis for both confirmed reschedule events is actual/360 (verified against workbook interest figures to sub-cent precision), matching the day_count_basis:360 field already used for QPSL's original fixture."
